The free <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/apple-invites/id6472498645">Apple Invites app</a> for the iPhone was updated today with three new features: shared albums now support full-resolution photo sharing, Image Playground now lets you create photorealistic backgrounds for invites, and guests who need to verify their email can now tap a link in their inbox instead of entering a code.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/General-Invites-App-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1068005" /><br/>
Released in February 2025, the Apple Invites app makes it easy to invite people to events, such as birthday parties and baby showers. The ability to create an event in the app requires subscribing to an iCloud+ plan with at least 50GB of storage for &#36;0.99 per month, but anyone who receives an event link can RSVP for free on any device.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's full release notes for version 1.12.0 of the app:<blockquote>• Shared Albums now support full-resolution sharing, so you can relive every moment in stunning detail right in the app. Anyone, including users without an Apple device, can join and contribute.<br/>
<br/>
• Image Playground now lets you create high quality backgrounds in pretty much any style, including photorealistic, so your invite captures exactly the vibe you have in mind.<br/>
<br/>
• Guests who need to verify their email can now tap a link in their inbox instead of entering a code, making it even easier to get into an event.<br/>
<br/>
